Implementing a text editor with multiple tabs (multitextlist) using Angular involves several steps:

### 1. Setting Up Your Project

First, make sure you have an Angular project set up. If not, create one using `ng new` or update your existing one.

```bash
ng new my-text-editor-app
cd my-text-editor-app
```

### 2. Creating the Multi-TextList Component

Create a component for managing the multitextlist functionality.

#### Step 2.1: Create the `MultiTextListComponent`

```bash
ng generate component multi-text-list
```

#### Step 2.2: Implement the `MultiTextListService`

In the generated component directory (`multi-text-list/src/app/multi-text-list/multi-text-list.service.ts`), create the service responsible for managing the multitextlist.

```typescript
// multi-text-list.service.ts
import { Injectable } from '@angular/core';

@Injectable({
  providedIn: 'root'
})
export class MultiTextListService {
  private texts = [];

  constructor() {}

  addText(text: string) {
    this.texts.push(text);
  }

  getText(index: number): string | undefined {
    return index < this.texts.length ? this.texts[index] : undefined;
  }

  deleteText(index: number) {
    if (index >= 0 && index < this.texts.length) {
      this.texts.splice(index, 1);
    }
  }
}
```

### 3. Adding the Text Editor Component

Now, let's create the main text editor component that will handle the UI and communication between the text list and the text editor.

#### Step 3.1: Create the `EditorComponent`

```bash
ng generate component editor
```

#### Step 3.2: Add the Text List Logic

In the `editor.component.html`, use the `MultiTextListService` to display the text list.

```html
<!-- editor.component.html -->
<app-multi-text-list [texts]="textList"></app-multi-text-list>
<textarea [(ngModel)]="currentText" placeholder="Type here..."></textarea>
<button (click)="saveText()">Save</button>
```

#### Step 3.3: Implement the `EditorComponent`

```typescript
// editor.component.ts
import { Component, OnInit, Input } from '@angular/core';
import { MultiTextListService } from './multi-text-list.service';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-editor',
  templateUrl: './editor.component.html',
  styleUrls: ['./editor.component.css']
})
export class EditorComponent implements OnInit {
  @Input() textList: string[] = [];
  currentText: string;

  constructor(private multiTextListService: MultiTextListService) {}

  ngOnInit(): void {
    // Initialize the currentText with the first text from the list
    this.currentText = this.textList[0];
  }

  saveText(): void {
    const newText = this.currentText.trim();
    if (!newText) {
      alert('Please type something before saving.');
      return;
    }

    this.multiTextListService.addText(newText);
    this.textList.unshift(this.currentText); // Add it at the beginning of the list
    this.currentText = ''; // Clear the input field
  }
}
```

